/*  The primaries — ParseCorePrimary in `src/Interpreter/Parser.cs`, and what it leans on: text
    with holes, call arguments, `cast`, record, series and object literals.

    ⚠ ParseCorePrimary is the largest method in that file. Its cases are ported here in the order
    the corpus uses them most, and anything not yet ported stops the file as `unsupported`, naming
    the token that opened it — so the parity test's list of unsupported files is also the list of
    what to write next.
*/

Pull a book on collections.
    Bind fact to looks-like-index-start, given (the text kind):
        For each opener in a series with ("Number", "String", "InterpolOpen", "Identifier", "It",
                "One", "LParen", "Article", "TrueKw", "FalseKw", "Minus"), repeat:
            If kind is opener, return true.
        Done.
        Return false.
    Done.

    /// OrdinalToIndex — `first` is 1 … `tenth` is 10, and `last` is nothing.
    Bind node to ordinal-index, given (the text lexeme):
        Define lowered as lexeme in lowercase.
        Define place as 0.
        For each ordinal in a series with ("first", "second", "third", "fourth", "fifth", "sixth",
                "seventh", "eighth", "ninth", "tenth"), repeat:
            Increment place by 1.
            If lowered is ordinal, return cast made on ("NumberLiteral", a series with (cast numeral on (place))).
        Done.
        Return cast nothing.
    Done.

    /// A 0x/0o/0b literal's digits, as the number they write.
    Bind number to bits-value, given (the text digits, the number radix):
        Define value as 0.
        Define spelled-digits as a chase.
        Insert digits in lowercase into spelled-digits.
        For each digit in spelled-digits, repeat:
            Define worth as (the position of digit in "0123456789abcdef") but void is 1.
            The value becomes value * radix + worth - 1.
        Done.
        Return value.
    Done.

    Bind node to bits-literal, given (the token written):
        Define shown-base as the characters from 2 to 2 of written's lexeme.
        Define digits as the characters from 3 to the end of written's lexeme.
        Define radix as 16 when shown-base is "x", otherwise (8 when shown-base is "o", otherwise 2).
        Define per-digit as 4 when shown-base is "x", otherwise (3 when shown-base is "o", otherwise 1).
        Return cast placed on ("BitsLiteral", a series with (
            cast numeral on (cast bits-value on (digits, radix)),
            cast quoted on (shown-base),
            cast numeral on (the length of digits * per-digit)), written).
    Done.

    Bind node or failure to core-primary unto parser:
        // `from <map>, the entry for <key>` — the map-first way to say a lookup.
        If cast one's peek-kind is "From":
            Define from-tok as cast one's advance.
            Cast one's skip-noise.
            If cast one's peek-kind is "Map":
                Cast one's advance.
                Cast one's skip-noise.
            Done.
            Define mapping as cast one's postfix or pass the failure off.
            Cast one's skip-noise.
            Cast one's consume on ("Comma") or pass the failure off.
            Cast one's skip-noise.
            Cast one's consume-word on ("entry") or pass the failure off.
            Cast one's skip-noise.
            Cast one's consume on ("For") or pass the failure off.
            Cast one's skip-noise.
            Define key as cast one's expression or pass the failure off.
            Return cast placed on ("MapLookup", a series with (mapping, key), from-tok).
        Done.

        // `the <name> of <thing>` — before the noise is skipped, so the `the` is still there.
        If cast one's is-word on ("the") and cast one's peek-kind is "Article" and cast one's is-named-access-pattern:
            Cast one's advance.
            Define name-tok as cast one's advance.
            Cast one's skip-noise.
            Cast one's advance.
            Cast one's skip-noise.
            Define whole as cast one's core-primary or pass the failure off.
            Return cast placed on ("RecordNamedAccess", a series with (cast quoted on (name-tok's lexeme), whole), name-tok).
        Done.

        Cast one's skip-noise.
        If cast one's is-word on ("text") and cast one's word-after-is on ("at"):
            Define text-tok as cast one's advance.
            Cast one's skip-noise.
            Cast one's advance.
            Cast one's skip-noise.
            Define address as cast one's core-primary or pass the failure off.
            Return cast placed on ("ForeignTextAt", a series with (address), text-tok).
        Done.

        Define tok as cast one's peek.
        Define kind as cast one's effective-kind on (tok).
        Define base as cast nothing.
        Define bracketed as false.

        If kind is "Number":
            Cast one's advance.
            Define amount as (tok's lexeme converted to number) but void is 0.
            The base becomes cast made on ("NumberLiteral", a series with (cast numeral on (amount))).
        Done.
        Otherwise if kind is "Bits":
            Cast one's advance.
            The base becomes cast bits-literal on (tok).
        Done.
        Otherwise if kind is "String":
            Cast one's advance.
            The base becomes cast made on ("StringLiteral", a series with (cast quoted on (tok's lexeme))).
        Done.
        Otherwise if kind is "Axiom":
            Cast one's advance.
            The base becomes cast placed on ("AxiomLiteral", a series with (cast quoted on (tok's lexeme)), tok).
            // ⚠ The raw text rides in `word`, which only a leaf prints — a `cufet` block is parsed again
            // from it, and the quoted form cannot be read back without ambiguity.
            The base's word becomes tok's lexeme.
        Done.
        Otherwise if kind is "InterpolOpen":
            Cast one's advance.
            The base becomes cast one's interpolated on (tok) or pass the failure off.
        Done.
        Otherwise if kind is "Identifier":
            Cast one's advance.
            The base becomes cast variable-named on (tok's lexeme, tok).
            If cast is-ordinal-lexeme on (tok's lexeme):
                Cast one's skip-noise.
                Define edge as cast spelled on (tok, "first") or cast spelled on (tok, "last").
                If edge and (cast one's peek-kind is "Number" or cast one's peek-kind is "LParen"):
                    Define count as cast one's addition or pass the failure off.
                    Cast one's skip-noise.
                    Cast one's consume-word on ("characters") or pass the failure off.
                    Cast one's skip-noise.
                    Cast one's consume on ("Of") or pass the failure off.
                    Cast one's skip-noise.
                    Define text-target as cast one's core-primary or pass the failure off.
                    The base becomes cast placed on ("TextSubstringEdge", a series with (
                        text-target, count, cast flag on (cast spelled on (tok, "first"))), tok).
                Done.
                Otherwise if cast one's peek-kind is "Of":
                    Cast one's advance.
                    Cast one's skip-noise.
                    Define target as cast one's core-primary or pass the failure off.
                    The base becomes cast placed on ("SeriesAccess", a series with (
                        target, cast ordinal-index on (tok's lexeme)), tok).
                Done.
            Done.
        Done.
        Otherwise if kind is "It":
            Cast one's advance.
            The base becomes cast variable-named on ("it", tok).
        Done.
        Otherwise if kind is "One":
            Cast one's advance.
            The base becomes cast variable-named on ("one", tok).
        Done.
        Otherwise if kind is "LParen":
            Cast one's advance.
            The base becomes cast one's expression or pass the failure off.
            Cast one's skip-noise.
            Cast one's consume on ("RParen") or pass the failure off.
            The bracketed becomes true.
        Done.
        Otherwise if kind is "Item":
            Cast one's advance.
            Cast one's skip-noise.
            If cast one's is-word on ("at") and cast one's kind-after is "LParen":
                Cast one's advance.
                Cast one's skip-noise.
                Cast one's consume on ("LParen") or pass the failure off.
                Cast one's skip-noise.
                Define row as cast one's expression or pass the failure off.
                Cast one's skip-noise.
                Cast one's consume on ("Comma") or pass the failure off.
                Cast one's skip-noise.
                Define column as cast one's expression or pass the failure off.
                Cast one's skip-noise.
                Cast one's consume on ("RParen") or pass the failure off.
                Cast one's skip-noise.
                Cast one's consume on ("Of") or pass the failure off.
                Cast one's skip-noise.
                Define grid as cast one's core-primary or pass the failure off.
                The base becomes cast placed on ("MatrixAccess", a series with (grid, row, column), tok).
            Done.
            Otherwise if cast looks-like-index-start on (cast one's peek-kind):
                Define index as cast one's expression or pass the failure off.
                Cast one's skip-noise.
                Cast one's consume on ("Of") or pass the failure off.
                Cast one's skip-noise.
                Define target as cast one's core-primary or pass the failure off.
                The base becomes cast placed on ("SeriesAccess", a series with (target, index), tok).
            Done.
            Otherwise:
                The base becomes cast variable-named on ("item", tok).
            Done.
        Done.
        Otherwise if kind is "NumberKw":
            Cast one's advance.
            Cast one's skip-noise.
            Cast one's consume on ("Of") or pass the failure off.
            Cast one's skip-noise.
            Define counted as cast one's core-primary or pass the failure off.
            The base becomes cast placed on ("SeriesLength", a series with (counted), tok).
        Done.
        Otherwise if kind is "Position":
            Cast one's advance.
            Cast one's skip-noise.
            Cast one's consume on ("Of") or pass the failure off.
            Cast one's skip-noise.
            Define part as cast one's expression or pass the failure off.
            Cast one's skip-noise.
            Cast one's consume on ("In") or pass the failure off.
            Cast one's skip-noise.
            Define whole as cast one's core-primary or pass the failure off.
            The base becomes cast placed on ("TextFind", a series with (part, whole), tok).
        Done.
        Otherwise if kind is "Characters":
            Cast one's advance.
            Cast one's skip-noise.
            Cast one's consume on ("From") or pass the failure off.
            Cast one's skip-noise.
            Define lower as cast one's addition or pass the failure off.
            Cast one's skip-noise.
            Cast one's consume on ("To") or pass the failure off.
            Define upper as cast nothing.
            If cast one's peek-kind is "End":
                Cast one's advance.
            Done.
            Otherwise if cast one's peek-kind is "Article" and cast one's kind-after is "End":
                Cast one's advance.
                Cast one's advance.
            Done.
            Otherwise:
                Cast one's skip-noise.
                The upper becomes cast one's addition or pass the failure off.
            Done.
            Cast one's skip-noise.
            Cast one's consume on ("Of") or pass the failure off.
            Cast one's skip-noise.
            Define whole as cast one's core-primary or pass the failure off.
            The base becomes cast placed on ("TextSubstringRange", a series with (whole, lower, upper), tok).
        Done.
        Otherwise if kind is "Replace":
            Cast one's advance.
            Cast one's skip-noise.
            Define old as cast one's addition or pass the failure off.
            Cast one's skip-noise.
            Cast one's consume on ("With") or pass the failure off.
            Cast one's skip-noise.
            Define fresh as cast one's addition or pass the failure off.
            Cast one's skip-noise.
            Cast one's consume on ("In") or pass the failure off.
            Cast one's skip-noise.
            Define whole as cast one's core-primary or pass the failure off.
            The base becomes cast placed on ("TextReplace", a series with (whole, old, fresh), tok).
        Done.
        Otherwise if kind is "Range":
            Cast one's advance.
            Cast one's skip-noise.
            Define lower as cast one's expression or pass the failure off.
            Cast one's skip-noise.
            Cast one's consume on ("To") or pass the failure off.
            Cast one's skip-noise.
            Define upper as cast one's expression or pass the failure off.
            Cast one's skip-noise.
            Define stride as cast nothing.
            If cast one's peek-kind is "Counting":
                Cast one's advance.
                Cast one's skip-noise.
                Cast one's consume on ("By") or pass the failure off.
                Cast one's skip-noise.
                The stride becomes cast one's expression or pass the failure off.
            Done.
            The base becomes cast placed on ("RangeExpression", a series with (lower, upper, stride), tok).
        Done.
        Otherwise if kind is "Void":
            Cast one's advance.
            The base becomes cast placed on ("VoidLiteral", a series of node, tok).
        Done.
        Otherwise if kind is "TrueKw" or kind is "FalseKw":
            Cast one's advance.
            The base becomes cast placed on ("BooleanLiteral", a series with (cast flag on (kind is "TrueKw")), tok).
        Done.
        Otherwise if kind is "Failure":
            Cast one's advance.
            Define next-kind as cast one's peek-kind.
            If next-kind is "String" or next-kind is "InterpolOpen" or next-kind is "Identifier" or next-kind is "LParen":
                Define message as cast one's expression or pass the failure off.
                Cast one's skip-noise.
                Define category-part as cast nothing.
                If cast one's peek-kind is "Of":
                    Cast one's advance.
                    Cast one's skip-noise.
                    Cast one's consume on ("Category") or pass the failure off.
                    Cast one's skip-noise.
                    The category-part becomes cast one's expression or pass the failure off.
                Done.
                The base becomes cast placed on ("FailureLiteral", a series with (message, category-part), tok).
            Done.
            Otherwise:
                The base becomes cast variable-named on ("the failure", tok).
            Done.
        Done.
        Otherwise if kind is "Exception":
            Cast one's advance.
            The base becomes cast variable-named on ("the exception", tok).
        Done.
        Otherwise if kind is "Cast":
            The base becomes cast one's cast-expression or pass the failure off.
        Done.
        Otherwise if kind is "Unbury":
            Cast one's advance.
            Cast one's skip-noise.
            Define stashed as cast one's unary-expr or pass the failure off.
            The base becomes cast placed on ("UnburyExpression", a series with (stashed), tok).
        Done.
        Otherwise if kind is "Series":
            The base becomes cast one's series-literal or pass the failure off.
        Done.
        Otherwise if kind is "Chase":
            Cast one's advance.
            The base becomes cast placed on ("ChaseLiteral", a series of node, tok).
        Done.
        Otherwise if kind is "Record":
            The base becomes cast one's record-literal or pass the failure off.
        Done.
        Otherwise if kind is "New":
            The base becomes cast one's object-literal or pass the failure off.
        Done.
        Otherwise:
            The base becomes cast one's rare-primary on (kind, tok) or pass the failure off.
        Done.

        // Possessive postfix: alice's name, one's field, alice's friend's name, math's floor.
        Cast one's skip-noise.
        While cast one's peek-kind is "Possessive", repeat:
            Define owns as cast one's advance.
            While cast one's peek-kind is "Article", repeat:
                Cast one's advance.
            Done.
            Define member as cast one's advance.
            The base becomes cast placed on ("PossessiveAccess", a series with (base, cast quoted on (member's lexeme)), owns).
            The bracketed becomes false.
            Cast one's skip-noise.
        Done.

        // A book member called with `of`: math's floor of x. Only a possessive, and never through
        // brackets.
        While bracketed is false and base's kind is "PossessiveAccess" and cast one's peek-kind is "Of", repeat:
            Define of-tok as cast one's advance.
            Cast one's skip-noise.
            Define args as cast listed.
            Define named as cast listed.
            If cast one's peek-kind is "LParen":
                Cast one's call-arguments on (args, named) or pass the failure off.
            Done.
            Otherwise:
                Define single as cast one's negation or pass the failure off.
                Cast args's add on (single).
            Done.
            The base becomes cast one's call-node on (base, args, named, of-tok).
            Cast one's skip-noise.
        Done.

        Return base.
    Done.

    /// `(CastExpression function [args] line column)`, with `:NamedArgs` when there are some.
    Bind node to call-node unto parser, given (the node callee, the node args, the node named, the token spot-tok):
        Define call as cast placed on ("CastExpression", a series with (callee, args), spot-tok).
        If the number of named's children is greater than 0:
            Cast call's add on (cast atom on (":NamedArgs")).
            Cast call's add on (named).
        Done.
        Return call.
    Done.

    // ── Text with holes ───────────────────────────────────────────────────

    Bind node or failure to interpolated unto parser, given (the token opener):
        Define result as cast nothing.
        Define started as false.
        While cast one's peek-kind is not "InterpolClose", repeat:
            Define piece as cast nothing.
            If cast one's peek-kind is "StringPiece":
                Define written as cast one's advance.
                The piece becomes cast made on ("StringLiteral", a series with (cast quoted on (written's lexeme))).
            Done.
            Otherwise if cast one's peek-kind is "InterpolHoleOpen":
                Define hole as cast one's advance.
                If cast one's peek-kind is "InterpolHoleClose":
                    Return a failure (cast one's refused on (hole, "empty interpolation '\{\}' — write an expression between the braces")).
                Done.
                Define inside as cast one's expression or pass the failure off.
                Cast one's consume on ("InterpolHoleClose") or pass the failure off.
                The piece becomes cast placed on ("TextConvert", a series with (inside), hole).
                Cast piece's add on (cast flag on (true)).
            Done.
            Otherwise:
                Return a failure (cast one's expecting on (cast one's peek, "string piece or interpolation expression")).
            Done.
            If started:
                The result becomes cast placed on ("TextJoin", a series with (result, piece), opener).
            Done.
            Otherwise:
                The result becomes piece.
                The started becomes true.
            Done.
        Done.
        Cast one's consume on ("InterpolClose") or pass the failure off.
        If started is false, return cast made on ("StringLiteral", a series with (cast quoted on (""))).
        Return result.
    Done.

    // ── Calls ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    /// IsNamedArgumentStart — a named field start with something after the name.
    Bind fact to is-named-argument-start unto parser:
        If cast one's is-named-field-start is false, return false.
        Define following as cast one's token-at on (cast one's past-noise on (one's at + 2)).
        Return following's kind is not "Comma" and following's kind is not "RParen".
    Done.

    Bind void or failure to one-call-argument unto parser, given (the node positional, the node named):
        If cast one's is-named-argument-start:
            Cast one's advance.
            Define name-tok as cast one's advance.
            Cast one's skip-noise.
            Define value as cast one's expression or pass the failure off.
            Define pair as cast listed.
            Cast pair's add on (cast quoted on (name-tok's lexeme)).
            Cast pair's add on (value).
            Cast named's add on (pair).
            Return.
        Done.
        If the number of named's children is greater than 0:
            Return a failure (cast one's expecting on (cast one's peek, "a named argument — once one argument is named, the ones after it must be too, "
                joined to "because position no longer says which parameter is meant")).
        Done.
        Cast one's skip-noise.
        Define value as cast one's expression or pass the failure off.
        Cast positional's add on (value).
    Done.

    Bind void or failure to call-arguments unto parser, given (the node positional, the node named):
        Cast one's consume on ("LParen") or pass the failure off.
        If cast one's kind-past-noise is not "RParen":
            Cast one's one-call-argument on (positional, named) or pass the failure off.
            Cast one's skip-noise.
            While cast one's peek-kind is "Comma", repeat:
                Cast one's advance.
                Cast one's one-call-argument on (positional, named) or pass the failure off.
                Cast one's skip-noise.
            Done.
        Done.
        Cast one's skip-noise.
        Cast one's consume on ("RParen") or pass the failure off.
    Done.

    Bind node or failure to cast-expression unto parser:
        Define cast-tok as cast one's consume on ("Cast") or pass the failure off.
        Define callee as cast one's postfix or pass the failure off.
        Cast one's skip-noise.
        Define args as cast listed.
        Define named as cast listed.
        If cast one's peek-kind is "On":
            Cast one's advance.
            Cast one's skip-noise.
            If cast one's peek-kind is not "LParen":
                If callee's kind is not "VariableReference":
                    Return a failure (cast one's refused on (cast-tok,
                        "identifier — method name must be a plain identifier in 'Cast method on receiver'")).
                Done.
                Define receiver as cast one's postfix or pass the failure off.
                Cast args's add on (receiver).
                Return cast one's call-node on (callee, args, named, cast-tok).
            Done.
            Cast one's call-arguments on (args, named) or pass the failure off.
            Return cast one's call-node on (callee, args, named, cast-tok).
        Done.
        If callee's kind is "CastExpression", return callee.
        Return cast one's call-node on (callee, args, named, cast-tok).
    Done.

    // ── Literals of several things ────────────────────────────────────────

    /// One field of a record or object literal: `the <name> <value>`, or a value by position.
    Bind void or failure to one-record-field unto parser, given (the node positional, the node named):
        If cast one's is-named-field-start:
            Cast one's advance.
            Define name-tok as cast one's advance.
            Cast one's skip-noise.
            Define value as cast one's expression or pass the failure off.
            Define pair as cast listed.
            Cast pair's add on (cast quoted on (name-tok's lexeme)).
            Cast pair's add on (value).
            Cast named's add on (pair).
            Return.
        Done.
        If the number of named's children is greater than 0:
            Return a failure (cast one's expecting on (cast one's peek,
                "positional fields must come before named fields — move all 'the name value' fields to the end")).
        Done.
        Define value as cast one's expression or pass the failure off.
        Cast positional's add on (value).
    Done.

    Bind void or failure to record-fields unto parser, given (the text closer, the node positional, the node named):
        If cast one's peek-kind is not closer:
            Cast one's one-record-field on (positional, named) or pass the failure off.
            Cast one's skip-noise.
            While cast one's peek-kind is "Comma", repeat:
                Cast one's advance.
                Cast one's one-record-field on (positional, named) or pass the failure off.
                Cast one's skip-noise.
            Done.
        Done.
        Cast one's consume on (closer) or pass the failure off.
    Done.

    Bind node or failure to record-literal unto parser:
        Define record-tok as cast one's consume on ("Record") or pass the failure off.
        Cast one's skip-noise.
        Cast one's consume on ("With") or pass the failure off.
        Cast one's skip-noise.
        Cast one's consume on ("LParen") or pass the failure off.
        Define positional as cast listed.
        Define named as cast listed.
        Cast one's record-fields on ("RParen", positional, named) or pass the failure off.
        Return cast placed on ("RecordLiteral", a series with (positional, named), record-tok).
    Done.

    Bind node or failure to object-literal unto parser:
        Define new-tok as cast one's advance.
        Cast one's skip-noise.
        Define name-tok as cast one's consume on ("Identifier") or pass the failure off.
        Cast one's skip-noise.
        Define args as cast listed.
        While cast one's peek-kind is "Of", repeat:
            Cast one's advance.
            Cast one's skip-noise.
            Define argument as cast one's type-annotation or pass the failure off.
            Cast args's add on (argument).
            Cast one's skip-noise.
        Done.
        Define positional as cast listed.
        Define named as cast listed.
        If cast one's peek-kind is "LBrace":
            Cast one's advance.
            Cast one's record-fields on ("RBrace", positional, named) or pass the failure off.
        Done.
        Return cast made on ("ObjectLiteral", a series with (cast quoted on (name-tok's lexeme), positional, named,
            cast row-of on (new-tok), cast column-of on (new-tok), args)).
    Done.

    Bind node or failure to series-literal unto parser:
        Define series-tok as cast one's advance.
        Cast one's skip-noise.
        Define annotation as cast nothing.
        If cast one's peek-kind is "Of":
            Cast one's advance.
            Cast one's skip-noise.
            If cast one's peek-kind is "Record" or cast one's is-word on ("records"):
                Cast one's advance.
                Cast one's skip-noise.
                Cast one's consume on ("Like") or pass the failure off.
                Cast one's skip-noise.
                The annotation becomes cast one's record-shape-body or pass the failure off.
            Done.
            Otherwise:
                The annotation becomes cast one's element-type on (false) or pass the failure off.
            Done.
            Cast one's skip-noise.
        Done.
        Define elements as cast listed.
        If cast one's peek-kind is "With":
            Cast one's advance.
            Cast one's skip-noise.
            Cast one's consume on ("LParen") or pass the failure off.
            Cast one's skip-noise.
            If cast one's peek-kind is not "RParen":
                Define first-element as cast one's expression or pass the failure off.
                Cast elements's add on (first-element).
                Cast one's skip-noise.
                While cast one's peek-kind is "Comma", repeat:
                    Cast one's advance.
                    Cast one's skip-noise.
                    Define element as cast one's expression or pass the failure off.
                    Cast elements's add on (element).
                    Cast one's skip-noise.
                Done.
            Done.
            Cast one's consume on ("RParen") or pass the failure off.
        Done.
        Return cast placed on ("SeriesLiteral", a series with (elements, annotation), series-tok).
    Done.
Done.
